	quest.1BEE2C09F14DC174.quest_subtitle: "Final Evolution • Mysticism"
	quest.1BEE2C09F14DC174.title: "Fallen ReaperAberration"
	quest.1BFAE1807CB9665B.quest_desc: [
		"&e&lWhat it does&r"
		"&fUnleash a primal fury and gain a massive physical boost to crush your enemies.&r"
		""
		"&a&lHow to get it&r"
		""
		"&f1. Reincarnation roll: leave the skill unlocked, reincarnate/reset, and roll the configured starting Unique Skill pool. World uniqueness and the server's skill-count/cost rules still apply.&r"
		""
		"&f2. Second-skill roll: this skill is also in the higher-priority second Unique Skill pool when that configured roll occurs.&r"
		""
		"&f3. Gluttony Steals addon: find a skill-bearing Goblin, Dwarf, Lizardman, Villager, Pillager, Wandering Trader, or MCA villager (10% default assignment chance; Wandering Traders are forced to Traveler), then land the killing blow with Gluttony's Mist mode. The mob's assigned Unique Skill is learned.&r"
		""
		"&f4. Defeat Awakened Feldway in Survival. If you have already exhausted his exclusive authority rewards, he rolls a random Unique skill you do not own instead. This skill is in that pool, but the result is random, normal learning restrictions still apply, and Feldway's reward is normally once per player.&r"
		""
		"&6&lMobs that use it&r"
		"&fCarrion (tensura_neb:carrion)&r"
		"&8A mob having the skill does not guarantee a drop. Use one of the learning methods above.&r"
		""
		"&3&lQuest tracking&r"
		"&f• Learn: Royal Beast — completes when you learn it&r"
		"&8These tasks only track progress; they never grant or evolve a skill.&r"
	]
	quest.1BFAE1807CB9665B.quest_subtitle: "Unique skill • TenSura: Reincarnated"
	quest.1BFAE1807CB9665B.title: "Royal Beast"
	quest.1C205C8886EC2A1A.quest_desc: [
		"&e&lLearn, equip, then activate&r"
		"&f1. Open the Status Menu with B and find the skill or ability page.&r"
		""
		"&f2. Place the skill into an active ability slot. Owning a skill does not automatically bind it to Z, X, or C.&r"
		""
		"&f3. Press the bound slot to activate it. Use Left Alt to move through that skill's modes; bind Previous Ability Mode if you want to move backward.&r"
		""
		"&f4. Toggle passive or sustained skills off when their cost or side effect is no longer useful. Some skills consume Aura/Magicules while active.&r"
		""
		"&f5. Keep using a learnable skill to build mastery. Learning, mastery, and evolution are separate states; the individual skill quest lists its confirmed route.&r"
	]
	quest.1C205C8886EC2A1A.title: "Using Skills Without Guesswork"
	quest.1C3829823C516E47.quest_desc: [
		"&e&lWhat you need&r"
